  The draft's reel_script, slides_spec and caption repeatedly lead with 'தீத்திபாளையம் திருப்பூர் குமரன் வீதி' and others; but the key issue: the draft says 'பேரூர்' is the location in headline, article's place of the incident is Maathampatti (hotel) and Perur police station - acceptable.
  The caption says 'அருண்குமார் வீட்டுக்குத் தப்பிச் சென்றார். ஆனால் இருவரும் பின்தொடர்ந்து சென்று' - the article says the two 'followed' him, consistent; however the caption's sentence 'அப்போது சாலையில் எச்சில் துப்பியபோது, தவறுதலாக ... மீது பட்டது' merges the spitting and the arrest-of-fact clearly, not a fabricated fact.
  The reel_script states the spitting happened 'இரவு' in the same sentence as the location of Perur in the opening line, and the opening sentence says 'இருவர் தாக்கியதால் போலீசார் கைது செய்தனர்' which is a garbled sentence: it reads as if the police arrested because of the assault, not clearly meaning the two were arrested after complaint; the phrasing is ungrammatical/unclear in Tamil.
  The reel_script omits that the victim's complaint was the basis of the case in a clear way only partly; more importantly the article's 'Perur' is the police station, but the draft's 'loc: பேரூர்' is fine.
  The caption's English line 'Perur assault after spitting incident, two arrested' is a fixed footer-like translation and not a problem, but the caption's '📰 முழு விவரம்' body mixes the spitting sentence with the 'மன்னிப்பு கேட்டார்' into a single sentence 'அப்போது சாலையில் எச்சில் துப்பியபோது, தவறுதலாக...' which combines two facts (spitting and the accidental hit) in a confusing way.
